Third-party software and models
------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product includes, depends on, and/or distributes third-party
software and machine-learning models. A full inventory of components,
their licenses, and required attributions is maintained in:

    THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md

The following attributions are highlighted here as required by their
respective licenses. This list is informational and does not modify the
Apache License under which this product is released.

* Speech recognition engine
    whisper.cpp and ggml (MIT), by ggml-org / Georgi Gerganov and
    contributors. https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp

* Speaker-diarization engine
    NeMo-Speech.cpp (Apache-2.0), by NVIDIA, statically linked with
    sentencepiece (Apache-2.0, Google). The upstream LICENSE, NOTICE, and
    THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are bundled with the engine.
    https://github.com/NVIDIA/NeMo-Speech.cpp

* Speech recognition model (downloaded at first setup)
    OpenAI Whisper large-v3-turbo (MIT), ggml conversion distributed via
    ggerganov/whisper.cpp.

* Voice activity detection model (downloaded at first setup)
    Silero VAD v6.2.0 (MIT, Silero Team), ggml conversion distributed via
    ggml-org/whisper-vad.

* Speaker-diarization model (downloaded at first setup; not bundled)
    NVIDIA Nemotron-3-Diarization, licensed under OpenMDW-1.1. The license
    text is provided in licenses/manual/ and can be viewed on the setup
    screen. https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Nemotron-3-Diarization

* Vulkan loader
    vulkan-1.dll from the LunarG Vulkan Runtime (Windows) and libvulkan.so.1
    from the Ubuntu 24.04 libvulkan1 package (Linux) (Apache-2.0, Khronos
    Group / LunarG), bundled unmodified so that the speech engines can start
    on PCs without a GPU driver or Vulkan loader. Version and source are
    recorded in resources/speech-engines/vulkan-loader/BUILD_INFO.txt.

* Audio decoding
    FFmpeg is used as a local command-line executable for audio decoding
    and format conversion. Windows builds bundle a BtbN FFmpeg "lgpl"
    build and treat it as LGPLv3 because the build includes
    --enable-version3. The bundled build is checked to exclude
    --enable-gpl, --enable-nonfree, libx264, libx265, libxvid, and
    libfdk-aac.
    Build project: https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds
    FFmpeg source: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg
    Build metadata and hashes are provided in resources/ffmpeg/
    FFMPEG_BUILD_INFO.txt. LoTT does not include PyAV ("av") or
    imageio-ffmpeg.

* C/C++ runtime (Linux builds)
    libgomp, the GCC OpenMP runtime library (GPL-3.0-or-later WITH
    GCC-exception-3.1, the GCC Runtime Library Exception), placed
    unmodified next to the speech engine executables in Linux builds.
    https://gcc.gnu.org/

* Linux media playback (AppImage only)
    Linux AppImage builds bundle GStreamer core and base/good/ALSA/
    PulseAudio plugins under the LGPL-2.1-or-later (with LGPL-compatible
    MIT/BSD components). GPL plugin sets, gst-libav, and faad are not
    bundled. https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org/

* C/C++ runtime
    Microsoft Visual C++ runtime libraries (Distributable Code), placed
    unmodified next to the speech engine executables.

* UI
    Angular and Angular Material (MIT), Tauri (MIT / Apache-2.0),
    Google Material Symbols font (Apache-2.0).

For the complete list and full license texts, see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
